<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania 27-day T-bill rate falls to 9.02 pct.</title>
<headline>Lithuania 27-day T-bill rate falls to 9.02 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rates on 27-day Lithuanian Treasury bills maintained a steady fall on Tuesday, hitting an average yield of 9.02 percent versus 9.59 percent at last week's</p>
<p>auction of 28-day paper, the nearest equivalent maturity.</p>
<p>Amounts are in millions of litas unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p> MATURITY    AV YLD (PCT)  LAST WEEK  MIN/MAX   ISSUE   BID</p>
<p> 27-day	 9.02	    9.59	8.50/9.27  55     125.0</p>
<p>The settlement date is September 13 and the bills mature on October 10.</p>
<p>--Riga Newsroom +3717-22 66 93</p>
</text>
